<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Merobaudes (poet)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Flavius Merobaudes</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Flavius Merobaudes was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> poet and Roman general of the 5th century. He wrote panegyrics for the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> and was honoured with a statue in the Forum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> in 435. In 443, succeeding his father-in-law Asturius, he commanded against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagaudae">Bagaudae</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> Tarraconensis before being recalled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p></div>
